WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:02.420
- So former president
Trump was actually able

00:00:02.420 --> 00:00:04.070
to get some lawyers to represent him

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:06.320
in the upcoming Senate impeachment trial.

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:08.340
Trump's new lawyers, David
Schoen and Bruce Castor,

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:10.410
seem to have a reasonable
professional background,

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:12.170
but as we've seen time and time again,

00:00:12.170 --> 00:00:13.870
sometimes having a reasonable background

00:00:13.870 --> 00:00:16.610
doesn't mean you're not
a MAGA hat crazy person.

00:00:16.610 --> 00:00:18.890
And here, one of the lawyers
is a solo practitioner

00:00:18.890 --> 00:00:20.710
who has been working with Roger Stone

00:00:20.710 --> 00:00:22.260
and is an Epstein truther,

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:23.680
and the other was a career prosecutor

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:25.340
who was also the former solicitor general

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:27.700
for Pennsylvania, which is a big wig job,

00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:29.740
but also apparently was
one of the prosecutors

00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:32.480
who did not prosecute Bill
Cosby in the early 2000s.

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:33.970
Of course, one of the lawyers
has already gone on TV

00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:36.400
and said the riots aren't
relevant to the impeachment trial.

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:38.810
- This has nothing to
do with President Trump.

00:00:38.810 --> 00:00:39.990
And the country doesn't need

00:00:39.990 --> 00:00:42.980
to just watch videos of riots and unrest.

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:45.300
- So it remains to be seen
whether they will go along

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:47.490
with former President
Trump's crazy strategy

00:00:47.490 --> 00:00:48.810
of saying that it was all justified

00:00:48.810 --> 00:00:50.610
and that it was all
based on election fraud.

00:00:50.610 --> 00:00:53.153
But subscribe, or I will see you in court.

